cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying preprint.
title: "Fidelity-Based Quantum Robustness Margins"
abstract: >-
  Toolbox for analysing (and optionally synthesising) piecewise-constant coherent
  quantum gate controllers under scalar structured Hamiltonian perturbations.
  Implements the gate-fidelity sensitivity bound, the Lipschitz constant it
  induces, and an iterative one-dimensional robustness margin certifying finite
  perturbations that preserve a prescribed fidelity threshold, with peer Python,
  Octave and Python implementations, cross-language consistency tests, and full
  reproduction of the accompanying paper's three-qubit case study. Also provides
  a supplementary comparison with the Kosut-Lidar-Rabitz fundamental bound
  (arXiv:2507.01215) specialised to this perturbation model.
type: software
